@Jc2k CI failed because I added a name() function to HomeKitNumber. Without the name(), the default name did not show the service name correctly in homeassistant. It was showing a generic name such as ecobee.number instead of ecobee.set_hold, where ecobee is the name of the thermostat. But this is causing tests for VOCOLINC to fail because it can not look up the name anymore.
Note that HomeKitButton was implemented with the name() function.
Was there any reason for HomeKitNumber to not override the name() function? Should I change the VOCOLINC test to use the new name, or just create a new class for the ecobee set hold entity?

